WEBVTT

00:15:57.034 --> 00:16:01.448
As a result, they often struggled
to adapt to and excel in their new roles.

00:16:01.472 --> 00:16:03.116
But others embraced it.

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:06.597
They'd observed their senior colleagues
being assertive with some clients

00:16:06.621 --> 00:16:08.173
while gently guiding others.

00:16:08.197 --> 00:16:10.616
And they'd experiment
with those provisional selves

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:11.994
to make them their own.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:15.149
The most successful
young professionals in her study

00:16:15.173 --> 00:16:17.866
weren't worried about
staying true to themselves.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:20.726
They were striving to develop themselves.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.580
HI: The knee-jerk reaction
is, "I'm fixed, this is who I am,

00:16:24.604 --> 00:16:29.176
and this is just not within
the realm of the possible."

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:30.952
And the minute you say to people,